problem: RPM packaging failed in release workflows because cargo-generate-rpm was fed a non-target-aware binary asset path and the workflows assumed a fixed output path
approach: Switched RPM metadata to a stable staging asset path (dist/axiom), copied the target-specific release binary there before cargo generate-rpm, and made both release workflows discover the generated .rpm dynamically before renaming it
failed_paths:
  - Tried target/%{_target}/release/axiom in Cargo.toml, but local cargo-generate-rpm rejected it as Asset file not found
verification:
  - cargo fmt --check
  - cargo test
  - git diff --check
  - cargo build --release --locked --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
  - cargo generate-rpm --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
  - find target -type f -path '*/generate-rpm/*.rpm' | sort
workflow_learning: When cargo-generate-rpm cannot interpolate the Rust target in asset metadata, stage the built binary into a stable path and make CI discover the produced rpm instead of assuming a fixed filename
related_files:
  - Cargo.toml
  - .github/workflows/release-beta-on-push.yml
  - .github/workflows/release.yml
